# Wave W17-AB (Foamline Path): foam floor — foam-flecked plank floor: sun-bleached pale planks laid along the road over bright water, their joints bright, carrying white foam flecks where the shallows slap the footings — the sea’s own signature drawn in the floor kind’s art, art layer only (design: a plank road over bright water, east of the white stone; the flowers at the end of it are not a rumour). Converts the shipped boardwalk entire — the causeway method (Ruling #4, second use): a causeway has no banks, so the planks ARE the path tier. Split from Route 218’s cause floor by weather entire (foam-white flecks in sun vs amber lamp-glow in rain) and from the shipped boardwalk it replaces by light: bleached and foamed vs plain harbour brown.
